==========================================
SYSADMIN DAY 03 NOTES — strace
Date: 16-10-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- strace shows every system call a program makes, in order, as it happens
- strace -c gives a summary table (syscall, count, time%) instead of the full firehose
- strace -e trace=<category> filters to just file, network, or specific named syscalls
- strace -p <PID> attaches to an ALREADY RUNNING process; Ctrl+C detaches without killing it
- A syscall returning -1 means failure; the E-code after it (EACCES, ENOENT...) is the exact reason
- EACCES = permission denied, ENOENT = file/path doesn't exist - look similar to the user, different underneath

COMMANDS / ACTIONS I PRACTICED:
[ ] strace ls /tmp  /  strace -c ls /tmp
[ ] strace -e trace=open,read,write,close ls /tmp
[ ] strace -e trace=network curl ...
[ ] sudo strace -p <PID> on a running sleep, then Ctrl+C to detach
[ ] comparing EACCES vs ENOENT on two different failures

paste or describe what you saw :
$ strace -c ls /tmp
